.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pons 1  "pons 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
pons \- pons asinorum — a falsifier\-first static analyzer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpons\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pons scans source without executing project code. Findings carry an evidence class; SPECULATIVE findings never gate a build. Exit codes: 0 completed below threshold, 1 threshold reached, 2 invalid input, no applicable input, failed required\-language coverage, or incomplete inventory with \-\-fail\-on\-skips. Additional extract/challenge adapters remain planned.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pons\-scan(1)
Scan a file or directory and report findings
.TP
pons\-catalogue(1)
Print the rule catalogue generated from the live registry
.TP
pons\-wharf\-trace(1)
Check supplied Wharf events against the bounded transfer model
.TP
pons\-validate\-report(1)
Validate a scan report; schema validity alone is not an assurance pass
.TP
pons\-man(1)
Generate a man page from the same command model as `\-\-help`
.TP
pons\-doctor(1)
Show optional adapter executables without claiming they are tested
.TP
pons\-trace(1)
Check an explicit ordered JSON event trace against a TOML protocol
.TP
pons\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
